# Build context exclusions.
#
# `infra/Dockerfile.api` does `COPY --from=builder /app/.venv /app/.venv` and
# then `COPY apps/api/ .`. Without this file that second copy includes the
# developer's local `apps/api/.venv` — which does not just bloat the image by
# hundreds of megabytes, it **overwrites the virtualenv built in the builder
# stage** with one compiled for the developer's own platform. A macOS arm64
# venv landing on a linux image produces a container that cannot start.
#
# So this is a correctness file, not an optimisation.

# --- virtualenvs (see above) ------------------------------------------------
**/.venv/
**/venv/

# --- python caches ----------------------------------------------------------
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.coverage
**/htmlcov/
**/*.egg-info/

# --- secrets — never in an image layer --------------------------------------
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
**/*.pem
**/*.key

# --- the Flutter client: not part of the API image --------------------------
apps/mobile/

# --- local data, backups, dumps ---------------------------------------------
backups/
**/*.dump
**/*.sqlite
**/*.sqlite3
**/*.sql.gz

# --- vcs, editors, os -------------------------------------------------------
.git/
.github/
**/.DS_Store
**/.idea/
**/.vscode/
**/*.swp

# --- docs and design material ------------------------------------------------
docs/
Velmart Mobile App Design System*/
*.md
!apps/api/README.md
